I have made a new version of the Convict role patch, incorporating
some of the excellent suggestions from this group:

http://nethack.edeca.net/karl/nethack-convict-0.2.diff

I would love to hear feedback from those who have tried the new
version.  The major changes include:

 * Convicts may now be Chaotic Humans, Dwarves, Gnomes, or Orcs.
Races that are normally friendly to them (e.g. gnomes and dwarves to
themselves and each other) are hostile to the Convict.

 * The convict's striped shirt starts as cursed, making it more of a
burden to him before he finds something to wear over it

 * Weapon and spell skills have been adjusted:

Basic: mace, short sword, matter spells

Skilled: dagger, dart, hammer, sling, two-weapon combat bare-handed
combat

Expert: club, flail, knife, pick-axe, escape spells

 * Quest artifact (the Iron Ball of Liberation) has been made lighter
(300 instead of 480), has been made Neutral for wishing purposes, and
does phasing instead of dig when invoked.  Phasing allows walking
through walls and stone like a Xorn for a limited amount of time.

 * Sick resistance is now granted at level 1, poison resistance at
level 7, and searching at level 20.

 * Vault guards also recognize the Convict from the wanted poster,
just like the Minetown watch

The quest has changed very little.  I'm interested in hearing what
people think of it as it stands now, but I am quite open to tweaking
it.

Questions:

 * Is the quest artifact good in its current state, or do people just
hate the concept of an artifact heavy iron ball?  I can do some
artifact pick instead if this is the case, I guess.

 * Is the quest too easy, too hard, too boring, etc?

 * Can anyone think of an artifact that would be a good first
sacrifice gift for this role?  Or can think of one to add to the
game?  This would be a good way to unrestrict e.g. long sword or broad
sword skill.


